==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|la|h₂erh₃}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*araō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*h₂éryeti||to plough}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*h₂erh₃-}}. The root-final laryngeal was lost in the Proto-Indo-European verb, but was restored in Proto-Italic.

Cognates include Ancient Greek {{m|grc|sc=polytonic|ἀρόω}}, Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|sc=Cyrs|орати}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|arti}}, and Old English {{m|ang|erian}} (archaic English {{m|en|ear}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-pronunc|arō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|arō|arāre|arāvī|arātum|conj=1}}

